    },
    {
      "id": "0018-anchor",
      "title": "anchor: where a floating drawing sits and how text wraps it",
      "since": "0.63.0",
      "tags": [
        "shared"
      ],
      "fn": "compare",
      "input": {
        "def": "anchor"
      },
      "expected": {
        "both": [],
        "lastWordOnly": [
          "allowOverlap",
          "horizontal",
          "vertical",
          "wrap"
        ],
        "finePrintOnly": []
      },
      "notes": "The anchor model agreed between last-word and Fancy before either built it, and shared with anchored pictures (CC-fancy-0055). allowOverlap is in the model (true by default). Absent, a drawing is inline. fine-print has none yet: a renderer that cannot place a floating drawing draws it inline at its paragraph and reports layout-not-preserved."
    },
